  "description": "A low-level codec for the Excel Binary Interchange File Format (BIFF5 and BIFF8) record streams found inside legacy .xls workbooks. A forward-only, allocation-free BiffReader walks physical records, detects the BIFF version, exposes every record's identifier and raw payload, and decodes the common structural and cell records through typed accessors — including the shared string table across its CONTINUE records — while a BiffWriter emits conformant BIFF5 or BIFF8 records from typed values or raw payloads. Understands how BIFF is encoded, not what an Excel workbook means: no compound-file container, no workbook or cell model, no formula evaluation.",
